63	\title{\textbf{The Conductor of the SIC-POVM Moduli Field:\\ A Cyclic Structure Across Arithmetic, Logic, and Machine}}
64	\author{C.\ Lando Mills%
65	\thanks{The author thanks Harry T.\ Larson; see Acknowledgements and \cite{Larson1961}.}}
66	\date{4 August 2026}
67	\maketitle
68	
69	\begin{abstract}
70	The squared magnitudes $N_k = |\psi_k|^2$ of a SIC-POVM fiducial vector in dimension $d$ generate an abelian extension of the real quadratic field $\Fd = \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{(d+1)(d-3)})$. This paper establishes that the conductor of this moduli field is the arithmetic expression of a single cyclic structure that also manifests as the Belnap trilattice in logic and as the self-hosting grammar of the IMASM machine substrate.
71	
72	At $d=2048$, the conductor collapses to the principal ideal $(16^3)\infty_1$. This is not a numerical coincidence. The sixteen states and three orderings of the trilattice, the $(16,3)$ torus knot on the horn torus, and the $16^3$ carrier of the IMASM native alphabet are all expressions of the same invariant. The moduli field is the ray class field at $\mathfrak{f}_d = \pt^{v_2(d)+1} \prod_{\mathfrak{p}\mid p, p|d} \mathfrak{p} \cdot \infty_1$, taken modulo the class group of $\Fd$, with exactly one infinite place ramified. At $d=16$, the $\sigma$-coinvariant count settles that the class group is not carried by the moduli; at $d=2048$ this yields degree $2^{21}$ over $\Fd$. The calibration dimensions $d=4,8,12$ are cross-sections where this structure becomes visible through exact fiducials. The Lean~4 formalization discharges the tower data to zero axioms, and the IMASM-native Replicating Code demonstrates the same fixed-point closure operationally: the grammar reads itself. The conductor, the trilattice, and the machine are one object.
73	\end{abstract}
74	
75	\noindent\textbf{Keywords:} SIC-POVM $\cdot$ moduli field $\cdot$ conductor $\cdot$ ray class field $\cdot$ Belnap trilattice $\cdot$ IMASM $\cdot$ Zauner conjecture $\cdot$ PARI/GP $\cdot$ Lean~4
76	
77	\newpage
78	\tableofcontents
79	\newpage
80	
81	%──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
82	\section{Introduction: The Cycle}
83	\label{sec:intro}
84	%──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
85	
86	A symmetric informationally complete positive operator-valued measure (SIC-POVM) in dimension $d$ is a set of $d^2$ unit vectors in $\mathbb{C}^d$ with equal pairwise overlap $|\langle\psi_j,\psi_k\rangle|^2 = 1/(d+1)$ for $j \neq k$. Zauner conjectured in 1999 that such configurations exist in every dimension, generated as orbits of a single fiducial under the Weyl--Heisenberg group~\cite{Zauner1999}. The conjecture remains open.
87	
88	Appleby, Bengtsson, Flammia, McConnell, and Yard established that fiducial coordinates are algebraic numbers in ray class fields of $\Fd = \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{\md})$, where $\md$ is the squarefree part of $(d+1)(d-3)$~\cite{Appleby2013,Appleby2017,AFMY2020}. This ties SIC existence to Hilbert's twelfth problem for real quadratic fields. But knowing the fiducial lives in \emph{some} ray class field is not knowing \emph{which}. The conductor determines the ray class group, the character count, and whether Stark machinery applies.
89	
90	This paper determines the conductor for the moduli $N_k = |\psi_k|^2$. But the determination is not linear. The conductor formula, the Belnap trilattice, and the IMASM machine grammar are not three separate results connected by interpretation. They are one structure expressing itself in three substrates: arithmetic, logical, and operational.
91	
92	The rule is stated in \Cref{conj:rule}. For even $d$, the moduli generate the ray class field of $\Fd$ at modulus
93	\[
94	    \mathfrak{f}_d = \pt^{v_2(d)+1} \cdot \prod_{\substack{p \mid d \\ p \text{ odd}}} \prod_{\mathfrak{p} \mid p} \mathfrak{p} \cdot \infty_1,
95	\]
96	with exactly one infinite place ramified, taken modulo the class group of $\Fd$. Its degree over $\Fd$ is $|\Cl_{\mathfrak{f}_d}|/h(\Fd)$.
97	
98	At $d=2048 = 2^{11}$, there are no odd prime divisors, $2$ is inert in $\Fd$, and the formula collapses to
99	\[
100	    \mathfrak{f}_{2048} = (2^{12})\infty_1 = (4096)\infty_1 = (16^3)\infty_1.
101	\]
102	The conductor is generated by sixteen cubed. This is the arithmetic face of the same structure whose logical face is the Belnap trilattice (sixteen states, three orderings) and whose operational face is the IMASM \Sixteen{} carrier and the self-hosting Replicating Code. The three are not analogous. They are identical.
103	
104	Three features of the answer matter more than the formula itself:
105	
106	\begin{enumerate}
107	    \item \textbf{Archimedean ramification.} Exactly one infinite place ramifies. The moduli field is real at the fiducial embedding but not totally real. PARI's \texttt{bnrstark} refuses it because standard Stark machinery requires total reality. The mixed-signature form is necessary: the unit at the conductor is recovered as a monomial in $S$-units of $\Fd$, which \Cref{sec:unit} carries out explicitly, rather than from a totally real Stark--Brumer construction that the signature forbids.
108	    

